      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0009-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000",
      "p0001-n0010-l0001",
      "p0001-n0010-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Due to the drought of southeast Australia, forest fires burn across the country, impacting New South Wales and eastern Victoria. To help Victoria government response to future wildfire disasters, we established the \u2018Rapid Bushfire Response\u2019 system."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000",
      "p0001-n0011-l0001",
      "p0001-n0011-l0002",
      "p0001-n0011-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For model 1, to address the irregularity of fire regions and SSA drones\u2019 information acquisition areas, we used regional discretization method, turning fire data and multi-drone cooperation in to con- straint equations. We then divide the information in discreated area into different layers, the drone layer and information layer indicate an SSA drone\u2019s different search mode and search zone, and the"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0006"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0006",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0007"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0004",
      "p0001-n0011-l0005",
      "p0001-n0011-l0006",
      "p0001-n0011-l0007"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "flame layer represents the severity of wildfire, we optimized SSA drone\u2019s search pattern balancing information detection revenue and SSA drone numbers. Finally, we optimized the location of EOC and repeater with the further obtained SSA drone location while considering communication con- strains and drones\u2019 traveling distance."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004",
      "p0001-n0012-l0005",
      "p0001-n0012-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For model 2, we discussed the changes in fire under global warming circumstances. We first formed a two-level function that maps temperature to average fire probability, and average fire probability to burned area size. To obtain the equation, we build cellular automata to simulate fire probability\u2019s effect on burned area and fitted the relation between temperature and fire probability. We then esti- mated the temperature variance due to climate change from further studies and calculated the esti- mated average fire probability of this year and the next decade. Finally, we simulated average fire scenes and estimated their fire severity."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005",
      "p0001-n0013-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For model 3, while referring to the number of SSA drones obtained without terrain conditions, we refined the regional discretization model to bring into the terrain influence. For SSA drones, we con- sidered topographical influence on a drone\u2019s traveling time and discussed path planning considering the varying time cost of different areas. As for repeaters, we evaluated the influence of terrain on communication, and measures a regions\u2019 communication shielding effect with the terrain\u2019s second gradient. We then further considered the reliability of communication and estimated the schedule change in different terrains."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Based on the above three models, we estimated that 10 SSA drones and 2 radio repeater drones is required to build the \u2018Rapid Bushfire Response\u2019 system. For next decade, the cost of imaging cameras and telemetry sensors (for SSA drones) will increase. We also suggest that while fire zone area has an influence on drone arrangements, topographical conditions plays a less important role."
  },
